// ADR 0153 decision 7 (BT-5155): the instance-field reflection selectors sent
// to a class from inside one of its own class methods, through `self`, in a
// block, and to the class held in a variable. Each raises the ordinary
// does-not-understand, as the same send from outside does.
// Fixture for class_field_reflection_dnu_test.bt.

Object subclass: ClassFieldReflectionProbe

  class selfFieldAt => self fieldAt: #x

  class selfFieldAtPut => self fieldAt: #x put: 1

  class selfHasField => self hasField: #x

  class selfClearField => self clearField: #x

  class selfHasFieldInBlock => [self hasField: #x] value

  class fieldAtOf: cls => cls fieldAt: #x

  // `run:` is process-bound (ADR 0142 §1 rule 3): it runs in the class's own
  // process, so a send there to the class reaches it from its own process.
  class run: aBlock => aBlock value
